  "data": "Namaz of Jafar-e-Tayyaar\nIt consists of four units with two Tashahhuds (i.e. the part of prayers in which the two creeds of Islam are recited) and two Taslims. In the first unit, Surahs al-Faatehah and al-Zalzalah are recited, in the second, Surahs al-Faatehah and al-A’adeyaat, in the third, Surahs al-Faatehah and al-Nasr, and in the fourth, Surahs al-Faatehah and al-Tawheed. In each unit, after the recitation of the Surahs and before the genuflection (ruku'), the following litany (Tasbihat) should be repeated fifteen times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ \nSUBHAANAL LAAHE WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE \nAll glory be to Allah, all praise be to Allah, \nوَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَاللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nWA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO.\nthere is no god save Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\nThe same litany (Tasbihat) is repeated, yet ten times only, during the Ruku’, after the Ruku’ while standing erect, during the prostration (Sujud), after the first Sajdah, during the second Sajdah, and after the second Sajdah. The same thing is repeated in all of the four units of the prayer. Hence, the litany will have been repeated three hundred times.\nShaykh al-Kulayni has narrated that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said to Abu Saeed al-Madaaeni, “May I teach you something that you should recite in Ja’far al-Tayyar’s Prayer?” As the man answered in the affirmative, the Imam (a.s.) said: After you say the Tasbihat in the second Sajdah of the fourth unit, say the following litany:\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَبِسَ الْعِزَّ وَالْوَقَارَ \nSUBHAANA MAN LABESAL I’ZZA WAL-WAQAARA \nGlory be to Him Who has dressed Himself dignity and sobriety! \nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ تَعَطَّفَ بِالْمَجْدِ وَتَكَرَّمَ بِهٖ \nSUBHAANA MAN TA-A’TTAFA BIL-MAJDE WA TAKARRAMA BEHI \nGlory be to Him Who has deigned and condescended with grandeur! \nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا يَنْبَغِي التَّسْبِيْحُ اِلَّا لَهٗ \nSUBHAANA MAN LAA YANBAGHIT TASBEEHO ILLAA LAHU \nGlory be to Him save Whom none is worthy of being glorified! \nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ اَحْصٰى كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمُهٗ \nSUBHAANA MAN AHSAA KULLA SHAY-IN I’LMOHU \nGlory be to Him Whose knowledge has counted all things! \nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْمَنِّ وَالنِّعَمِ \nSUBHAANA ZIL MANNE WAN-NE-A’ME \nGlory be to the Lord of bounty and boon! \nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْقُدْرَةِ وَالْكَرَمِ \nSUBHAANA ZIL QUDRATE WAL KARAME \nGlory be to the Lord of omnipotence and nobility! \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِمَعَاقِدِ الْعِزِّ مِنْ عَرْشِكَ \nALLAHUMMA INNE AS-ALOKA BE-MA-A’AQEDIL I’ZZE MIN A’RSHEKA \nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of the objects of dignity in Your Throne, \nوَ مُنْتَهَى الرَّحْمَةِ مِنْ كِتَابِكَ وَاسْمِكَ الْاَعْظَمِ \nWA MUNTAHAR RAHMATE MIN KETAABEKA WAS-MEKAL A-A’ZAME \nin the name of the utmost of mercy in Your Book, and in the name of Your Greatest Name \nوَكَلِمَاتِكَ التَّامَّةِ الَّتِيْ تَمَّتْ صِدْقًا وَعَدْلًا \nWA KALEMAATEKAT TAAAM-MATIL LATEE TAMMAT SIDQAN WA A’DLAN \nand Your Accomplished Words, which have been accomplished truly and justly, \nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ.\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AHLE BAYTEHI.\nsend blessings to Muhammad and his Household.\nThen, you may mention your needs in the form of supplication.\nShaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus both narrated that al-Mufaddal ibn ‘Umar said that he heard Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) saying the following supplicatory prayer after accomplishing Ja’far al-Tayyar’s Prayer:\nيَا رَبِّ\nYAA RABBE, YAA RABBE\nO LORD, O LORD!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nيَا رَبَّاهُ يَا رَبَّاهُ\nYAA RABBAAHO, YAA RABBAAHO\nO my Lord, O my Lord!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nرَبِّ رَبِّ\nRABBE, RABBE\nLord, Lord!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nيَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHO, YAA ALLAAHO\nO Allah, O Allah!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nيَا حَيُّ يَا حَيُّ\nYAA HAYYO, YAA HAYYO\nO Ever-living, O Ever-living!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nيَا رَحِيْمُ يَا رَحِيْمُ\nYAA RAHEEMO, YAA RAHEEMO\nO All-merciful, O All-merciful!\nSay it as many times as possible in one breath.\nيَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ\nYAA RAHMAANO, YAA RAHMAANO\nO All-compassionate, O All-compassionate!\nRepeat it seven times.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEEN\nO Most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nRepeat it seven times.\nThen, say the following:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَفْتَتِحُ الْقَوْلَ بِحَمْدِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AFTATEHUL QAWLA BE HAMDEKA \nO Allah, I begin my speech with Your praise, \nوَاَنْطِقُ بِالثَّنَاءِ عَلَيْكَ \nWA ANTEQO BIS-SANAAA-E A'LAYKA \nI speak by extolling You, \nوَاُمَجِّدُكَ وَلَا غَايَةَ لِمَدْحِكَ \nWA OMAJJEDOKA WA LAA GHAAYATA LE-MADHEKA \nand I glorify You, and there is no limit to Your praise. \nوَاُثْنِي عَلَيْكَ وَمَنْ يَبْلُغُ غَايَةَ ثَنَائِكَ وَاَمَدَ مَجْدِكَ\nWA USNEE A'LAYKA WA MAN YABLOGHO GHAA-YATA SANAAA-EKA WA AMADA MAJDEKA \nI laud You—and who can reach the limit of Your laudation or the extent of Your glory? \nوَاَنّٰى لِخَلِيْقَتِكَ كُنْهُ مَعْرِفَةِ مَجْدِكَ \nWA ANNAA LE-KHALEEQATEKA KUNHO MA'REFATE MAJDEKA \nAnd how can Your creatures ever recognize Your glory [in its actual measure]! \nوَاَيَّ زَمَنٍ لَمْ تَكُنْ مَمْدُوحًا بِفَضْلِكَ \nWA AYYA ZAMANIN LAM TAKUN MAMDOOHAN BE-FAZLEKA \nAnd how can there be any moment for which You do not deserve praise due to Your favors \nمَوْصُوفًا بِمَجْدِكَ عَوَّادًا عَلٰى الْمُذْنِبِيْنَ بِحِلْمِكَ \nMAWSOOFAN BE-MAJDEKA A'WWAADAN A'LAL MUZNEBEENA BE-HILMEKA \nand in which You are not ascribed to glory and in which You do not incessantly treat the sinful with Your forbearance? \nتَخَلَّفَ سُكَّانُ اَرْضِكَ عَنْ طَاعَتِكَ \nTAKHALLAFA SUKKAANO ARDHEKA A'N TAA-A'TEKA \nAlthough the inhabitants of Your earth have fallen behind in being obedient to You, \nفَكُنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ عَطُوفًا بِجُودِكَ جَوَادًا بِفَضْلِكَ \nFA-KUNTA A'LAYHIM A'TOOFAN BE JOODEKA JAWAADAN BE FAZLEKA \nYou have been kind to them out of Your munificence, munificent out of Your favors, \nعَوَّادًا بِكَرَمِكَ يَا لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nA'WWAADAN BE KARAMEKA YAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTAL \nand liberal out of Your generosity. O He save Whom there is no god! \nالْمَنَّانُ ذُو الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nMANNAANO ZUL JALAALE WAL IKRAAM. \nO All-benevolent! O Lord of Glory and Honour!",
  "merits": "Ja’far al-Tayyar’s Prayer is as precious as gold, since it is the most magnificent recommended devotional rite. Altogether with its great merits the most important of which is that it erases major sins, this prayer has been reported through authenticated chain of authority. The best time of its performance is the first hours of daylight on Fridays. ",
