    "Special Namaz\nAl-Mufazzal then added: Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) then said to me, “If you have a significant request and you want it to be granted, you may offer this prayer, say this supplication, and implore Almighty Allah to respond to you. If you do, it will be granted, Allah willing.”\nShaykh al-Tusi has narrated that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) recommended the following supplicatory prayer for having one’s requests granted:\nObserve fasting on consecutive Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. At Thursday evening, give half bushel of food for ten poor people as alms. On Friday, wash yourself and go out to a wasteland and offer therein Ja’far al-Tayyaar’s Prayer sticking your knees to the ground after you uncover them. You may then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nيَا مَنْ اَظْهَرَ الْجَمِيْلَ وَ سَتَرَ الْقَبِيْحَ \nYAA MAN AZHARAL JAMEELA WA SATARAL QABEEHA \nO He Who has shown only goodness and concealed the evil (deeds of His servants)!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يُؤَاخِذْ بِالْجَرِيْرَةِ \nYAA MAN LAM YO-AAKHIZ BIL-JAREERATE \nO You who do not seize based on crime \nوَ لَمْ يَهْتِكِ السِّتْرَ يَا عَظِيْمَ الْعَفْوِ \nWA LAM YAHTEKIS SITRA YAA A'ZEEMAL A'FWE \nand do not tear the veil; O Great in Forgiveness; \nيَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ يَا وَاسِعَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ \nYAA HASANAT TAJAAWOZE YAA WAASE-A'L MAGHFERATE \nO Excellent in Overlooking; O Vast in Pardon; \nيَا بَاسِطَ الْيَدَيْنِ بِالرَّحْمَةِ \nYAA BAASETAL YADAYNE BIR-RAHMATE \nO Extender of hands with mercy; \nيَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰى وَ مُنْتَهٰى كُلِّ شَكْوٰى \nYAA SAAHEBA KULLE NAJWAA WA MUNTAHAA KULLE SHAKWAA \nO Listener of every secret and Goal of every complaint; \nيَا مُقِيْلَ الْعَثَرَاتِ يَا كَرِيْمَ الصَّفْحِ \nYAA MOQEELAL A’SARAATE YAA KAREEMAS SAF-HE \nO Granter of reprieves from lapses; O Noble in Forbearing; \nيَا عَظِيْمَ الْمَنِّ يَا مُبْتَدِئًا بِالنِّعَمِ قَبْلَ اسْتِحْقَاقِهَا \nYAA A'ZEEMAL MANNE YAA MUBTADEAN BIN-NE-A'ME QABLAS TEH-QAAQEHAA \nO Great in Bestowal; O Initiator of blessings before they are deserved; \nيَا رَبَّاهُ يَا رَبَّاهُ يَا رَبَّاهُ،\nYAA RABBAAHO YAA RABBAAHO YAA RABBAAHO.\nO My Lord, O My Lord, O My Lord.\nRepeat this statement ten times.\nيَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHO YAA ALLAAHO YAA ALLAAHO\nO Allah, O Allah, O Allah!\nRepeat it ten times, too.\nيَا سَیِّدَاهُ يَا سَيِّدَاهُ\nYAA SAYYEDAAHO YAA SAYYEDAAHO\nO my Master, O my Master! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا مَوْلَايَاهُ،يَا مَوْلَايَاهُ\nYAA MAWLAAYAAHO, YAA MAWLAAYAAHO\nO my Chief, O my Chief! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا رَجَآئَاهُ\nYAA RAJAAA-AAHO\nO my hope! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا غِيَاثَاهُ\nYAA GHEYAASAAHO\nO my succor! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا غَايَةَ رَغَبَتَاهُ\nYAA GHAAYATA RAGHBATAAHO\nO ultimate of my desire!\nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا رَحْمٰنُ\nYAA RAHMAANO\nO All-beneficent! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا رَحِيْمُ\nYAA RAHEEMO\nO All-merciful! \nRepeat it ten times.\nيَا مُعْطِىَ الْخَيْرَاتِ\nYAA MO’TEYAL KHAYRAATE\nO Giver of fortunes! \nRepeat it ten times.\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَثِيْرًا طَيِّبًا \nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN KASEERAN TAYYEBAN\nBless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as much as \nكَاَفْضَلِ مَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلٰى اَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nKA-AFZALE MAA SALLAYTA A’LAA AHADIN MIN KHALQEKA\nand as decently as You have ever blessed any of Your creatures.\nYou may then mention your requests.\nMany narrations have mentioned emphatically fasting on these three days and then performance of a two-unit prayer at midday (zohr) on Friday so that one’s requests are granted."
